From ed34eb822f1c6dd4de5ddd11e6ace9a195ca5c00 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Poovendhan Selvaraj <poovendh@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 22 Jun 2026 15:52:43 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] ovl: fix null-ptr-deref in ovl_i_path_real() when upper mount
 is NULL

A null pointer dereference is observed in ovl_permission() at offset
0x150/0x190 on ARM64:

  BUG: KASAN: null-ptr-deref in ovl_permission+0x150/0x190
  Read of size 8 at addr 0000000000000018 by task modprobe/23238

The crash address 0x18 corresponds to the mnt_idmap field of struct
vfsmount (offset 24 bytes), meaning realpath.mnt is NULL when
mnt_idmap(realpath.mnt) is called in ovl_permission().

In ovl_i_path_real(), when the inode has an upper dentry, path->mnt is
set to ovl_upper_mnt(OVL_FS(inode->i_sb)). ovl_upper_mnt() returns
ofs->layers[0].mnt, which is NULL when the overlay has no upper layer
(read-only overlay). In this case path->dentry is non-NULL but
path->mnt is NULL, causing the crash in the caller.

Additionally, if lowerpath is NULL (no lower paths) and path->dentry
is also NULL, the existing code would crash on lowerpath->dentry.

Fix both cases in ovl_i_path_real():
- Guard lowerpath dereference with a NULL check
- If ovl_upper_mnt() returns NULL, clear path->dentry so the function
  returns NULL, triggering the existing -ECHILD guard in callers
  (ovl_permission() returns -ECHILD for RCU retry)

Change-Id: I2ffbca9a9ea6dd44246de7ff2b5df63be765b30d
Signed-off-by: Poovendhan Selvaraj <poovendh@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 fs/overlayfs/util.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/fs/overlayfs/util.c b/fs/overlayfs/util.c
index 0da1cd01d01c..8028102ab87b 100644
--- a/fs/overlayfs/util.c
+++ b/fs/overlayfs/util.c
@@ -343,10 +343,12 @@ struct inode *ovl_i_path_real(struct inode *inode, struct path *path)
 
 	path->dentry = ovl_i_dentry_upper(inode);
 	if (!path->dentry) {
-		path->dentry = lowerpath->dentry;
-		path->mnt = lowerpath->layer->mnt;
+		path->dentry = lowerpath ? lowerpath->dentry : NULL;
+		path->mnt = lowerpath ? lowerpath->layer->mnt : NULL;
 	} else {
 		path->mnt = ovl_upper_mnt(OVL_FS(inode->i_sb));
+		if (unlikely(!path->mnt))
+			path->dentry = NULL;
 	}
 
 	return path->dentry ? d_inode_rcu(path->dentry) : NULL;
-- 
2.34.1

